Once the algorithm fills a byte, its value is final because all later stores have been considered first. A simple implementation takes \(O(kw)\) work for \(k\) visited stores and load width \(w\); an interval overlap routine can avoid scanning disjoint bytes. The endian assumption belongs to both encoding and assembly. If the load itself is observable or may fault, even exact reconstruction of its bytes cannot justify deleting it.
